Description: Take the volume monitor before the desktop is made
 The desktop replaces its folder as it starts (DesktopWindow::setDesktopFolder), which can drop
 libfm-qt's last reference to GLib's volume monitor while one of libfm-qt's job threads gets a new
 one. GLib's unix mount monitor can then deadlock in g_context_specific_group_request_state: the
 desktop's main thread waits forever, holds org.pcmanfm.PCManFM without answering, and never draws
 the desktop. The application's own reference, taken from the start, keeps the monitor alive
 across that moment.
Author: solarex1
Forwarded: https://github.com/lxqt/pcmanfm-qt/pull/2213
Last-Update: 2026-10-30
---
--- a/pcmanfm/application.cpp
+++ b/pcmanfm/application.cpp
@@ -345,6 +345,14 @@
 }
 
 int Application::exec() {
+
+    // Take the volume monitor before the desktop is made, and keep it, as below. The desktop
+    // replaces its folder as it starts, which can drop libfm-qt's last reference to the
+    // monitor while one of its job threads gets a new one; GLib's mount monitor can then
+    // deadlock in g_context_specific_group_request_state, and the desktop never draws.
+    if(isPrimaryInstance) {
+        volumeMonitor_ = g_volume_monitor_get();
+    }
 
     if(!parseCommandLineArgs()) {
         return 0;
@@ -354,7 +362,9 @@
         setQuitOnLastWindowClosed(false);
     }
 
-    volumeMonitor_ = g_volume_monitor_get();
+    if(!volumeMonitor_) {
+        volumeMonitor_ = g_volume_monitor_get();
+    }
     // delay the volume manager a little because in newer versions of glib/gio there's a problem.
     // when the first volume monitor object is created, it discovers volumes asynchronously.
     // g_volume_monitor_get() immediately returns while the monitor is still discovering devices.
